id=a52sxq_wireless_dex
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Samsung DeX entry points lead to wireless DeX
author=CodesRahul96
description=UNTESTED-ON-DEVICE. One UI 9 DeX is desktop windowing on an external display; on a phone it is started wirelessly by the launcher's ConnectivityActivity (Smart View/Miracast connection with SemWifiDisplayConfig mode 2, which system_server turns into an external desktop display). The framework and WMShell side is the same as on the S26U once desktop windowing is on (sff.sh). But the launcher's DeX quick settings tile only takes the wireless path when /sys/class/dp_sec/dex exists, i.e. on a phone with DisplayPort alt mode; the A52s kernel has no CONFIG_SEC_DISPLAYPORT, so the tile would take the tablet "DeX on this screen" branch (stand-alone desktop windowing on the phone screen, which cannot host desktops). Launcher: its "Supports dp" check returns true, so the tile opens the wireless device list. Settings: ExternalDisplayUtils.isWirelessDexOnlyDevice() is pinned to true (stock already returns true on a phone without dp_sec/dex): Connected devices > Samsung DeX is shown with the wireless-only help text. SystemUI: the DeX tile stays available and in the stock default tile list (stock; asserted so no other patch hides it). This patch is the only owner of the DeX entry points; a52s_hw_features no longer touches them. Nothing changes until DeX is started; wired DeX stays impossible (no DP alt mode).
